# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Ambient — environment configuration
#
# THERE ARE NO SECRETS IN THIS PROJECT, AND THIS FILE EXISTS TO SAY SO.
#
# The prototype has no backend, makes no network calls and holds no API keys,
# tokens or credentials of any kind. There is nothing to authenticate against.
# You do not need to create a .env to build or run it.
#
# The two things a developer does configure are below, and neither is a secret.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# 1. Android SDK location.
#    Written by Android Studio into local.properties, which is gitignored.
#    Only needed for a command-line build on a machine that has never opened
#    the project in Android Studio.
#
# ANDROID_SDK_ROOT=/path/to/Android/sdk

# 2. On-device model weights (OPTIONAL).
#    Not a credential, not shipped, not in the APK, not in this repository:
#    ~304 MB of Gemma 3 270M weights obtained under the Gemma Terms of Use and
#    pushed to the device by hand. See README "The model is not in the repo".
#
#    Without it the narrator falls back to templates and the app runs fully.
#
#    Expected on the device at:
#    /sdcard/Android/data/eu.feg.ambient/files/models/gemma3-270m-it-q8.litertlm
